{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>Two and twenty thousand.</b> When you sum the details you find they exceed by three hundred. Some say that Scripture took a short route, mentioning the thousands and omitting the hundreds, but this is impossible because the surplus numbers are less than three hundred. The truth is the words of tradition: a firstborn does not displace a firstborn, and the meaning of the verse is: all the counted of the Levites, apart from the firstborn. And Judah HaParsi was precise to bring proof from the number, that the firstborn of the Levites are part of the seventy-three Levites, and when you take in this number from the counted of Israel, and afterwards take the number of the counted Levites who come to the army, corresponding to the counted of the Levites from a month old, they will be close — but he has said nothing, for Israel were counted from twenty years old with no other limit, while the Levites were counted from thirty to fifty, and there is a great difference between them. We rely only on the words of tradition."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:12.153080750Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}